PianoTouch is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). What it takes from other work, and from where:

NativeGeniSpi (UniXNU, github.com/Droid-VM/UniXNU, drivers/NativeGeniSpi, b5399b5646c4d7415deec6d887fd51715a97a024; the UniXNU
catalog's QcomGeniSpi lineage), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  GeniSpi.c (sha256 2042cfc9647391e24d5a558202046425ac62a05adfc73afe769367b8374e3f91), GeniSpi.h (sha256
  e73891e4571c5323bca27aaf987bafa002856dfa1dcee156ff31b119e2d3ae3c) and Test/geni-spi.c as tests/geni_spi_host.c (sha256
  a5b8a9ab217590064fc8ce701ceee5f2dcfbc0b3f0b0d8907505bae25fb2c113): copied unchanged. The GENI SPI master (FIFO and SE DMA modes,
  polled), its register model test.

Project-SunUEFI (unixnu-research/Project-SunUEFI, main 4ef87402e9d58465af871e4c4f4a5de87599d81c), BSD-2-Clause-Patent (file headers):
  uefi/components/touch-product/PianoTouchService.c (sha256 f1ba8aba2e2e7abd80b32586c5c807fe8d7a7e972c66aa537b8de8dcd2bcead1)
    piano's bring-up order (engine reset, the trim loop over three hw-register tables, the download with the hardware CRC, reset
    state 0xa0..0xaf, calibration 0xa3, the operating-mode command, the GPIO162 edge latch), the pins (MISO/MOSI/CLK/CS on
    GPIO40-43, lcd-id GPIO100: 0 CSOT, 1 BOE; IRQ GPIO162), SPI by hand on those pins (mode 0, pull/drive settings, 64-byte read
    windows), the handshake (0x77) and watchdog (0xfd/0xfe) transport blocks and the re-download after ten of the latter.
    Re-expressed in Nt36532.h and PianoTouch.cpp; its EFI clock protocol, AbsolutePointer and release paths are not taken.
  uefi/components/touch-product/PianoTouchNvt.c (sha256 291511315d1ae227c881772a459db48a45ee5ad8ff858c82e490490ae8185ea9) and .h
    (sha256 16840ba55ffe0776db89a588a1de5a878325801fdbdfaa2e508e3d7bfec9425d): the image layout (the NVT/MOD sector, the version
    byte, ILM/DLM/info/overlay records, the word CRC) and the chip tables (trim IDs, memory maps): parseImage, crc32Words, kHwRegs.
  uefi/components/touch-product/PianoTouchMatrix.c (sha256 d407e60639253aa973db7e6dd93f2f17201206c8e6c1068bcb4c76d89cb30950) and .h
    (sha256 6d080362e3e46bf796b3d406bfaf6809143d785a995a013aabaa1aca0aa3e567): the matrix decoder (type lock, median reference, line
    noise, peaks, centroid, tracking, the panel mapping with Y flipped) and the packet checksum, ported to TouchMatrix.h /
    Nt36532.h; the tip debounce on top is new. Its physical evidence (SunUEFI tools/prepare_product.py backend_status): firmware
    loaded and an idle baseline established over GPIO SPI on piano; touching broke the frame checksums (GPIO SPI too slow).

UniXNU-Odin3 (unixnu-research/UniXNU-Odin3, main 6d58c09d1529fb22dba8e3d6f74d8d4c7f9f8306), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  modules/Pagani/drivers/PaganiInput/PaganiInput.cpp (sha256 d6363b9fde015a70f9741aa3a175f49243935e306e94adba5e970385aade68c3)
    the OnePlus 13T's SPI touch on SM8750 QUP1 (SE4): SE DMA with the FIFO disabled through QUP1's stream 0xa3, the contiguous DMA
