  tools/extract-thp-calibration.py (sha256 a8845a8ee56b3ad31bf7077c62c70c923d38c47fb7f5009bedba3a707a05d0a0), MIT: makes the
    private calibration file from the vendor piano_nova_<panel>_thp_config.ini; not run here. The file itself (per unit) is never
    committed, its arrays never printed: the build embeds it from the ignored out/ tree and logs its panel and an 8-digit hash prefix.

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoDwc3/SmmuStream.h: included as it is (-I package/PianoDwc3) for stream 0xa3's bypass context bank.
  package/PianoKeyboard (PianoKeyboardHID; provenance in package/PianoInput/UPSTREAM: macOS-DroidVM 11ac316 overlay/kext/DroidVMInput,
    sha256 f05d9d9912b1ae5b57000dcc49f6a4539410e5212c34b31aa4270e31cfac8afc): the IOHIDDevice subclass, its publication from start
    and the event-service notification, the codeless IOHIDEventDriver personality and the vtable check of
    tooling/k27/kext/PianoTouch.json; the TLMM pin handling (eGPIO claim, the rising-edge latch with the GIC delivery off), the step
    and boot-argument layout. The tablet report's shape (absolute X/Y 0..32767 and buttons) is the source HID class's tablet mode
    (the same file); TouchHid.h's descriptor is written from the HID 1.11 specification and the Usage Tables.
  package/PianoKeyboard/HidDescriptors.h (makeTouchpadDescriptor) and docs/drivers/keyboard.md §6a: the scroll resolution declared
    through the Wheel's physical extents (Unit inch, Unit Exponent -3, the integer quotient IOHIDEventService takes) and fine counts
    in place of a Resolution Multiplier, re-used in TouchHid.h makeTouchDescriptor; the scroll direction convention (fingers up =
    wheel up, right = AC Pan right) and the axis lock rule (one axis at least twice the other).
  package/include/PianoPowerContract.h: the two power states and pianopower::join (the contract of docs/power.md §4), included.
  New for this package (2026-11-11), no outside source: TouchTrack.h (the multi-contact tracker, the hysteresis, the palm rejection),
  TouchGesture.h (the gestures), TouchPower.h (suspend and the display off), TouchPace.h's no-edge reads and BurstHold, Nt36532.h's
  probeState. Facts behind TouchPower.h: piano's Ubuntu (docs/ubuntu-history/device.md §2.10, kernel.md: the THP stream after
  panel enable and stopped at disable, touch transfers stopped before the SPI bus suspends, an asynchronous restart, touch no wake
  source).

Facts only, no code (their licences do not allow reuse here):
